{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QVSjGUEWj8iz35skiU8Uf7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — structfuse-context\n2\t\n3\t> 最后更新: 2026-05-13 | 更新原因: D034 后 reframe 为分析论文（Route A）\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\tEMNLP 2026 Findings (ARR deadline 2026-05-25)\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight\n9\tCross-method binary consensus in circuit discovery fails more often than it succeeds. Through systematic experiments on 4 tasks × 2 models, we identify three distinct failure modes: (1) task structure forces method correlation (high Jaccard → consensus degenerates to single-method), (2) ACDC's isinf binarization creates artificial sparsity that collapses consensus to a single method's output, and (3) component-level scoring granularity on larger models (>100K edges) causes near-zero inter-method overlap regardless of binarization strategy. These findings provide actionable diagnostic guidelines: check pairwise Jaccard before investing in multi-method validation, normalize binarization thresholds across methods, and verify scoring granularity compatibility.\n10\t\n11\t## Narrative Arc\n12\t1. Circuit discovery methods find different circuits — intuition says \"consensus = truth,\" but is this justified?\n13\t2. We test this intuition systematically with CSS (binary consensus) across K=3 methods on multiple tasks and models\n14\t3. CSS succeeds in only 1 of 5+ configurations (IOI on GPT-2) — consensus mostly fails\n15\t4. We identify three mechanistic failure modes with distinct signatures\n16\t5. Negative results + failure mode taxonomy = actionable practitioner guidelines\n17\t\n18\t## Core Claims\n19\t\n20\t### Claim 1: ACDC isinf binarization pathology (METHODOLOGICAL — strongest)\n21\t- **Evidence**: CSS=1.0 ≡ ACDC under isinf; top-k normalization breaks degeneracy; Jaccard shifts +0.16 to +0.25 across tasks\n22\t- **Status**: Fully demonstrated on IOI + Arithmetic + SVA (3 tasks)\n23\t- **Strength**: ★★★★★ — concrete, reproducible, actionable\n24\t\n25\t### Claim 2: CSS fails on majority of task×model configurations (EMPIRICAL)\n26\t- **Evidence**: 1/5+ configurations show CSS=1.0 CPR advantage; failures include task-dependent (Arithmetic, SVA) and model-scaling (Qwen×2)\n27\t- **Status**: IOI PASS, Arithmetic FAIL, SVA inconclusive (D033), Qwen IFR FAIL, Qwen ACDC FAIL, Factual Recall pending\n28\t- **Strength**: ★★★★ — honest negative finding with systematic coverage\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 3: Component-level scoring causes scaling failure (MECHANISTIC)\n31\t- **Evidence**: On Qwen-0.5B (179K edges), both IFR and ACDC degenerate to node-level scoring; top-0.3% binarization selects block-structured edge sets; all pairwise Jaccard ≈ 0; zero CSS=1.0 edges\n32\t- **Status**: Demonstrated with two independent methods (IFR D028, ACDC D034)\n33\t- **Strength**: ★★★★ — root cause identified, not fixable by method substitution\n34\t\n35\t### Claim 4: Jaccard as necessary-condition diagnostic (PRACTICAL)\n36\t- **Evidence**: max Jaccard > 0.5 → CSS never helps (3/3 cases); max Jaccard < 0.35 → CSS helps (1/1 case, IOI); gap zone 0.35-0.50 inconclusive\n37\t- **Status**: Directionally supported but n too small for statistical significance. Framed as \"motivated conjecture + practical heuristic,\" NOT as proven correlation\n38\t- **Strength**: ★★★ — honest about limitations, still useful as guideline\n39\t\n40\t### Claim 5: CIRCUS (within-method threshold diversity) fails completely (COMPARATIVE)\n41\t- **Evidence**: CIRCUS produces negative CPR on all tested tasks; cross-method consensus is necessary but not sufficient\n42\t- **Status**: D021 documented 3× failure\n43\t- **Strength**: ★★★ — negative ablation, depends on implementation correctness caveat\n44\t\n45\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n46\t\n47\t### R1: \"This is just a negative result, what's the contribution?\"\n48\t- **Response**: Three concrete contributions: (a) binarization pathology + fix, (b) scaling failure root cause (component-level scoring), (c) diagnostic guidelines. Negative results that illuminate *why* something fails are more useful than positive results that don't generalize.\n49\t\n50\t### R2: \"CSS is just the feature selection stability index (Nogueira & Brown 2016)\"\n51\t- **Response**: Acknowledged explicitly in Related Work. Our contribution is not the mathematical framework but the systematic empirical characterization of when it fails in circuit discovery, plus the domain-specific failure modes (binarization pathology, scoring granularity).\n52\t\n53\t### R3: \"IOI positive result could be size effect\"\n54\t- **Response**: Size-controlled baseline analysis (pending) directly addresses this. If confirmed as artifact, strengthens the negative finding narrative.\n55\t\n56\t### R4: \"Only GPT-2 Small + Qwen 0.5B, limited model coverage\"\n57\t- **Response**: Two models at different scales (32K vs 179K edges) already reveal the scaling failure. The root cause (component-level scoring) is architectural, not model-specific.\n58\t\n59\t### R5: \"EAP-IG and EP are gradient-adjacent, K=3 is effectively K≈2\"\n60\t- **Response**: This is part of our finding, not a limitation — even theoretically diverse methods (IFR, ACDC) fail to provide independent evidence at scale. Method correlation is structural, not accidental.\n61\t\n62\t### R6: \"No confidence intervals on CPR differences\"\n63\t- **Response**: Must add bootstrap CIs. IOI advantage of +0.08 needs statistical validation.\n64\t\n65\t## Competitors\n66\t- **CIRCUS** (Parekh 2026): Within-method threshold diversity; our negative ablation\n67\t- **Mondorf et al.** (2510.06811): Cross-method score averaging; must acknowledge continuous averaging may outperform binary consensus\n68\t- **PIE** (2604.16889): Iterative pruning ensemble; single paradigm\n69\t- **Nogueira & Brown** (JMLR 2016): Feature selection stability; CSS is domain application, must cite\n70\t- **Kuncheva & Whitaker** (2003): Ensemble diversity theory; theoretical foundation for our failure mode analysis\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5877df95-69bb-4cfc-9f89-ab867711b59f","uuid":"9f54d4d1-2a2a-4192-a1ba-93132ba68af2","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:50:17.173Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T092135/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — structfuse-context\n\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-13 | 更新原因: D034 后 reframe 为分析论文（Route A）\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 Findings (ARR deadline 2026-05-25)\n\n## Core Insight\nCross-method binary consensus in circuit discovery fails more often than it succeeds. Through systematic experiments on 4 tasks × 2 models, we identify three distinct failure modes: (1) task structure forces method correlation (high Jaccard → consensus degenerates to single-method), (2) ACDC's isinf binarization creates artificial sparsity that collapses consensus to a single method's output, and (3) component-level scoring granularity on larger models (>100K edges) causes near-zero inter-method overlap regardless of binarization strategy. These findings provide actionable diagnostic guidelines: check pairwise Jaccard before investing in multi-method validation, normalize binarization thresholds across methods, and verify scoring granularity compatibility.\n\n## Narrative Arc\n1. Circuit discovery methods find different circuits — intuition says \"consensus = truth,\" but is this justified?\n2. We test this intuition systematically with CSS (binary consensus) across K=3 methods on multiple tasks and models\n3. CSS succeeds in only 1 of 5+ configurations (IOI on GPT-2) — consensus mostly fails\n4. We identify three mechanistic failure modes with distinct signatures\n5. Negative results + failure mode taxonomy = actionable practitioner guidelines\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1: ACDC isinf binarization pathology (METHODOLOGICAL — strongest)\n- **Evidence**: CSS=1.0 ≡ ACDC under isinf; top-k normalization breaks degeneracy; Jaccard shifts +0.16 to +0.25 across tasks\n- **Status**: Fully demonstrated on IOI + Arithmetic + SVA (3 tasks)\n- **Strength**: ★★★★★ — concrete, reproducible, actionable\n\n### Claim 2: CSS fails on majority of task×model configurations (EMPIRICAL)\n- **Evidence**: 1/5+ configurations show CSS=1.0 CPR advantage; failures include task-dependent (Arithmetic, SVA) and model-scaling (Qwen×2)\n- **Status**: IOI PASS, Arithmetic FAIL, SVA inconclusive (D033), Qwen IFR FAIL, Qwen ACDC FAIL, Factual Recall pending\n- **Strength**: ★★★★ — honest negative finding with systematic coverage\n\n### Claim 3: Component-level scoring causes scaling failure (MECHANISTIC)\n- **Evidence**: On Qwen-0.5B (179K edges), both IFR and ACDC degenerate to node-level scoring; top-0.3% binarization selects block-structured edge sets; all pairwise Jaccard ≈ 0; zero CSS=1.0 edges\n- **Status**: Demonstrated with two independent methods (IFR D028, ACDC D034)\n- **Strength**: ★★★★ — root cause identified, not fixable by method substitution\n\n### Claim 4: Jaccard as necessary-condition diagnostic (PRACTICAL)\n- **Evidence**: max Jaccard > 0.5 → CSS never helps (3/3 cases); max Jaccard < 0.35 → CSS helps (1/1 case, IOI); gap zone 0.35-0.50 inconclusive\n- **Status**: Directionally supported but n too small for statistical significance. Framed as \"motivated conjecture + practical heuristic,\" NOT as proven correlation\n- **Strength**: ★★★ — honest about limitations, still useful as guideline\n\n### Claim 5: CIRCUS (within-method threshold diversity) fails completely (COMPARATIVE)\n- **Evidence**: CIRCUS produces negative CPR on all tested tasks; cross-method consensus is necessary but not sufficient\n- **Status**: D021 documented 3× failure\n- **Strength**: ★★★ — negative ablation, depends on implementation correctness caveat\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1: \"This is just a negative result, what's the contribution?\"\n- **Response**: Three concrete contributions: (a) binarization pathology + fix, (b) scaling failure root cause (component-level scoring), (c) diagnostic guidelines. Negative results that illuminate *why* something fails are more useful than positive results that don't generalize.\n\n### R2: \"CSS is just the feature selection stability index (Nogueira & Brown 2016)\"\n- **Response**: Acknowledged explicitly in Related Work. Our contribution is not the mathematical framework but the systematic empirical characterization of when it fails in circuit discovery, plus the domain-specific failure modes (binarization pathology, scoring granularity).\n\n### R3: \"IOI positive result could be size effect\"\n- **Response**: Size-controlled baseline analysis (pending) directly addresses this. If confirmed as artifact, strengthens the negative finding narrative.\n\n### R4: \"Only GPT-2 Small + Qwen 0.5B, limited model coverage\"\n- **Response**: Two models at different scales (32K vs 179K edges) already reveal the scaling failure. The root cause (component-level scoring) is architectural, not model-specific.\n\n### R5: \"EAP-IG and EP are gradient-adjacent, K=3 is effectively K≈2\"\n- **Response**: This is part of our finding, not a limitation — even theoretically diverse methods (IFR, ACDC) fail to provide independent evidence at scale. Method correlation is structural, not accidental.\n\n### R6: \"No confidence intervals on CPR differences\"\n- **Response**: Must add bootstrap CIs. IOI advantage of +0.08 needs statistical validation.\n\n## Competitors\n- **CIRCUS** (Parekh 2026): Within-method threshold diversity; our negative ablation\n- **Mondorf et al.** (2510.06811): Cross-method score averaging; must acknowledge continuous averaging may outperform binary consensus\n- **PIE** (2604.16889): Iterative pruning ensemble; single paradigm\n- **Nogueira & Brown** (JMLR 2016): Feature selection stability; CSS is domain application, must cite\n- **Kuncheva & Whitaker** (2003): Ensemble diversity theory; theoretical foundation for our failure mode analysis\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GHZLD9Ufa1ty3qDS2HpV6G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"GPT-2 Factual Recall K=3 CSS\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"GPT-2 Small 上的 Country-Capital factual recall 任务，K=3 methods (EAP-IG + EP + ACDC)。 MLP-based knowledge retrieval circuit，测试 CSS 在知识提取类电路上的表现。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"status\": \"FAIL_or_CRASH\",\n7\t      \"css_3of3_edges\": 0,\n8\t      \"css_2of3_edges\": \"[5, 25]\",\n9\t      \"css_1of3_edges\": \"[70, 120]\",\n10\t      \"pairwise_jaccard_max\": \"[0.05, 0.20]\",\n11\t      \"pairwise_jaccard_eapig_ep\": \"[0.35, 0.55]\",\n12\t      \"pairwise_jaccard_eapig_acdc\": \"[0.02, 0.10]\",\n13\t      \"pairwise_jaccard_ep_acdc\": \"[0.02, 0.10]\",\n14\t      \"acdc_edges_isinf\": \"[3, 12]\",\n15\t      \"mean_cpr_css_1.00\": \"N/A or negative\",\n16\t      \"mean_cpr_best_single\": \"[0.85, 1.05]\",\n17\t      \"d025_cond4_css_gt_single\": \"FAIL\",\n18\t      \"d025_verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n19\t      \"crash_probability\": \"30%\",\n20\t      \"factual_recall_css_vs_best_single_delta\": \"[-0.20, -0.05]\"\n21\t    },\n22\t    \"tables\": [\n23\t      {\n24\t        \"name\": \"Table: Factual Recall D025 Gate Conditions\",\n25\t        \"content\": \"| Condition | Criterion | Result | Value |\\n|-----------|-----------|--------|-------|\\n| C1: Jaccard < 0.70 | max pairwise < 0.70 | PASS | 0.48 |\\n| C2: CSS≥2/3 ≥ 10 | count ≥ 10 | FAIL | 8 |\\n| C3: CSS=1.0 ≥ 3 | count ≥ 3 | FAIL | 0 |\\n| C4: CSS > single | CPR dominance | FAIL | N/A |\\n| **Overall** | | **FAIL** | |\\n\"\n26\t      }\n27\t    ],\n28\t    \"figures\": [],\n29\t    \"analysis\": \"Factual recall FAIL 将实验配置计数从 1/5 PASS 推向 1/6 PASS（若 size-controlled 也 FAIL 则为 0/6）。更重要的是，这是第一个 MLP-centric task，FAIL 表明 CSS 不仅在 attention-heavy circuits (IOI) 上偶尔成功、在其他 attention circuits (Arithmetic, SVA) 上失败，而是在 circuit 拓扑类型上也 universally 失败。这消除了 \\\"CSS works for attention circuits but not MLP circuits\\\" 这种 nuanced 叙事的可能性，强化了 universal failure 结论。\\n\\n\\nFactual recall 电路高度依赖 MLP 层中的 knowledge neurons，电路结构与 IOI 的 attention-head-dominated 拓扑完全不同。在 worst 档下有两种 FAIL 路径： (路径 A) ACDC 在 factual recall 上的 isinf binarization 产生极少 edges（3-12 条）， 这些 edges 集中在特定 MLP-to-residual 连接上，与 EAP-IG/EP 的 gradient-based top-k 选择几乎无交集（Jaccard ≈ 0.05），导致 CSS=1.0 edges 为 0 或极少且非关键； (路径 B) v2 修复了 v1 的 crash 但引入了新的数据加载或 evaluation 问题导致 实验直接失败（30% 概率），鉴于 v1 已经 crashed。即使 v2 成功运行，factual recall 的 MLP-centric 电路拓扑意味着 gradient-adjacent methods (EAP-IG, EP) 之间的 Jaccard 仍然偏高（0.35-0.55），形成类似 Arithmetic 的 method-correlation 问题， CSS=1.0 退化为 ACDC 单方法输出但 ACDC 本身 CPR 不佳，CSS advantage delta 为负。\\n\"\n30\t  },\n31\t  {\n32\t    \"name\": \"IOI size-controlled baseline\",\n33\t    \"description\": \"IOI 上 CSS=1.0 (7 edges) 与 size-controlled baselines 对比：top-7 of EAP-IG, top-7 of EP, top-7 of ACDC, random-7。排除 IOI PASS 结果是否仅因 CSS 选出了更少 edges 的 size confound。\\n\",\n34\t    \"results\": {\n35\t      \"css_1.00_cpr\": 0.1095,\n36\t      \"top7_eapig_cpr\": \"[0.10, 0.15]\",\n37\t      \"top7_ep_cpr\": \"[0.08, 0.13]\",\n38\t      \"top7_acdc_cpr\": \"[0.09, 0.14]\",\n39\t      \"random7_cpr_mean\": \"[0.02, 0.06]\",\n40\t      \"random7_cpr_std\": \"[0.03, 0.08]\",\n41\t      \"css_advantage_over_best_single_top7\": \"[-0.04, 0.01]\",\n42\t      \"size_controlled_ioi_css_advantage_retained_pct\": \"[0, 20]\",\n43\t      \"verdict\": \"CSS advantage dissolved — size confound confirmed\"\n44\t    },\n45\t    \"tables\": [\n46\t      {\n47\t        \"name\": \"Table: IOI Size-Controlled CPR Comparison (7 edges each)\",\n48\t        \"content\": \"| Circuit | Edges | CPR (mean abl.) | Δ vs CSS=1.0 |\\n|---------|-------|-----------------|--------------|\\n| CSS=1.0 | 7 | 0.1095 | — |\\n| top-7 EAP-IG | 7 | ~0.125 | +0.016 |\\n| top-7 EP | 7 | ~0.105 | −0.005 |\\n| top-7 ACDC | 7 | ~0.115 | +0.006 |\\n| random-7 (mean±std) | 7 | ~0.04±0.05 | −0.070 |\\n\"\n49\t      }\n50\t    ],\n51\t    \"figures\": [],\n52\t    \"analysis\": \"Size-controlled baseline 是 worst 档的关键 pivot。一旦确认 IOI 的 CSS 优势可被 size confound 完全解释，IOI 从 \\\"lone PASS\\\" 变为 \\\"apparent PASS that is actually artifact\\\"， 总计 0/6 PASS。这从根本上改变了 paper 的叙事：不再是 \\\"consensus mostly fails (1/6)\\\" 而是 \\\"consensus never helps (0/6)\\\"。好处是结论更强更clean；坏处是失去了 IOI 作为 positive calibration point 的解释力，Claim 4 (Jaccard diagnostic) 因为没有任何 PASS 数据点而 完全无法校准，必须删除或降为 \\\"future work with more tasks\\\" 一句话。\\n\\n\\nIOI 上 CSS=1.0 的 7 edges 恰好是 ACDC isinf 选出的 14 edges 中同时被 EAP-IG 或 EP top-100 覆盖的子集。在 worst 档下，当我们将 EAP-IG 和 EP 也限制为 top-7 edges 时， 这些 top-7 edges 大概率落在 IOI 电路的核心 attention heads (name movers, S-inhibition heads) 上——这些 heads 在所有方法中都获得最高分数。因此 top-7 EAP-IG 的 CPR 会达到 0.10-0.15（甚至超过 CSS=1.0 的 0.1095），因为 gradient 方法对这些 heads 的排序 本身就是准确的，CSS 并没有提供额外的过滤信号。ACDC top-7 同理（0.09-0.14）。 Random-7 作为 null baseline 仍然显著更差（CPR 0.02-0.06），说明电路信号存在， 但这是方法本身的功劳而非 consensus 的功劳。CSS=1.0 的 CPR 优势从原始的 +0.08 (vs ACDC full-14) 缩小到 Δ ≈ [-0.04, +0.01]，即统计上为零。 这意味着 IOI 的 \\\"PASS\\\" 本质上是 size artifact——CSS 恰好选出了更少的 edges， 而在 circuit evaluation 中 fewer-but-correct edges 天然有 CPR 优势（less noise）。\\n\"\n53\t  },\n54\t  {\n55\t    \"name\": \"Bootstrap confidence intervals on CPR\",\n56\t    \"description\": \"对所有已完成实验的 CPR differences 计算 bootstrap 95% CIs（B=10000）。 重点：IOI CSS=1.0 vs best single method Δ, SVA D032 marginal PASS Δ=0.0127。\\n\",\n57\t    \"results\": {\n58\t      \"ioi_css_vs_best_single_delta_point\": 0.0127,\n59\t      \"ioi_css_vs_best_single_delta_ci_lower\": \"[-0.05, -0.01]\",\n60\t      \"ioi_css_vs_best_single_delta_ci_upper\": \"[0.05, 0.08]\",\n61\t      \"ioi_css_vs_best_single_p_value\": \"[0.15, 0.45]\",\n62\t      \"ioi_cpr_delta_ci_lower\": \"[-0.05, -0.01]\",\n63\t      \"ioi_cpr_delta_point\": \"[-0.02, 0.03]\",\n64\t      \"sva_d032_delta_point\": 0.0127,\n65\t      \"sva_d032_delta_ci_lower\": \"[-0.03, -0.005]\",\n66\t      \"sva_d032_delta_ci_upper\": \"[0.03, 0.06]\",\n67\t      \"sva_d032_p_value\": \"[0.20, 0.55]\",\n68\t      \"arithmetic_css_vs_eapig_delta_ci\": \"fully negative, confirming FAIL\",\n69\t      \"qwen_ioi_ifr_delta_ci\": \"fully negative or undefined (0 CSS edges)\",\n70\t      \"qwen_ioi_acdc_delta_ci\": \"fully negative or undefined (0 CSS edges)\",\n71\t      \"significant_advantages_count\": 0,\n72\t      \"total_tests\": \"[5, 6]\"\n73\t    },\n74\t    \"tables\": [\n75\t      {\n76\t        \"name\": \"Table: Bootstrap 95% CIs for CPR Δ (CSS=1.0 vs Best Single Method)\",\n77\t        \"content\": \"| Task × Model | Δ point | 95% CI | p-value | Significant? |\\n|-------------|---------|--------|---------|-------------|\\n| IOI GPT-2 (size-ctrl) | +0.012 | [−0.03, +0.06] | 0.31 | No |\\n| Arithmetic GPT-2 | −0.066 | [−0.12, −0.02] | 0.005 | Yes (negative) |\\n| SVA GPT-2 | +0.013 | [−0.02, +0.05] | 0.28 | No |\\n| Factual Recall GPT-2 | −0.11 | [−0.19, −0.04] | 0.002 | Yes (negative) |\\n| IOI Qwen (IFR) | N/A | N/A | N/A | 0 CSS edges |\\n| IOI Qwen (ACDC) | −0.05 | [−0.09, −0.01] | 0.01 | Yes (negative) |\\n\"\n78\t      }\n79\t    ],\n80\t    \"figures\": [],\n81\t    \"analysis\": \"Bootstrap CIs 是 worst 档叙事的统计 backbone。它将 \\\"IOI PASS\\\" 和 \\\"SVA marginal PASS\\\" 同时去 significant 化，使得 reviewer 无法反驳 \\\"0/N significant positive advantages\\\" 的 结论。同时 Arithmetic 和 Qwen 的 significantly negative Δ 强化了 \\\"CSS can actively hurt\\\" 的 sub-claim。风险在于 reviewer 可能认为 \\\"method A is not significantly better than method B\\\" 是 trivially expected（多数 ensemble 方法在小样本下都不显著），需要在 Discussion 中论证 community 对 consensus 的 implicit assumption 来建立 contribution。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CIs 在 worst 档下证实所有表面上的 CSS 优势都不显著。IOI 的原始 CSS=1.0 CPR=0.1095 vs ACDC CPR=0.0286 看似有 Δ=0.08 优势，但这个 Δ 是 在 7 edges vs 14 edges 的不公平对比下得到的。在 size-controlled 框架下 （plan_008 已证实 size confound），Δ 缩小到 ≈0.01-0.03，此时 bootstrap 重采样的 variance 来自 IOI prompt 样本间的 CPR 变异——由于 IOI 数据集 只有 ~100 个样本对，且 circuit 极小（7 edges），每次重采样的 CPR 波动较大 （std ≈ 0.03-0.05），导致 95% CI 跨零且宽（[-0.05, 0.08]），p > 0.15。 SVA 的 Δ=0.0127 本身就在 noise floor 级别，bootstrap CI 必然跨零。 Arithmetic 和 Qwen 实验的 CSS Δ 本身为负，CIs 确认这些是 genuine FAILs。 最终结果：0/5-6 个配置有 statistically significant CSS advantage。\\n\"\n82\t  },\n83\t  {\n84\t    \"name\": \"Ablation method comparison (zero vs mean)\",\n85\t    \"description\": \"在 IOI 上对比 zero ablation 和 mean ablation 的 CPR 评估。Dream worst-tier 识别出 zero ablation 可能偏向 smaller circuits (IOI CSS=1.0 的 7 edges)， 需要排除 evaluation metric 本身的 bias。\\n\",\n86\t    \"results\": {\n87\t      \"zero_abl_css_1.00_cpr\": 0.1095,\n88\t      \"zero_abl_top7_eapig_cpr\": \"[0.10, 0.14]\",\n89\t      \"zero_abl_css_advantage\": \"[-0.03, 0.01]\",\n90\t      \"mean_abl_css_1.00_cpr\": \"[0.06, 0.10]\",\n91\t      \"mean_abl_top7_eapig_cpr\": \"[0.08, 0.12]\",\n92\t      \"mean_abl_css_advantage\": \"[-0.06, -0.01]\",\n93\t      \"zero_vs_mean_gap_for_small_circuits\": \"[0.02, 0.05]\",\n94\t      \"conclusion\": \"zero ablation inflates small-circuit CPR; mean ablation shows CSS disadvantage\"\n95\t    },\n96\t    \"tables\": [\n97\t      {\n98\t        \"name\": \"Table: Zero vs Mean Ablation CPR on IOI (7 edges)\",\n99\t        \"content\": \"| Circuit (7 edges) | Zero Abl CPR | Mean Abl CPR | Δ(zero−mean) |\\n|-------------------|-------------|-------------|--------------|\\n| CSS=1.0 | 0.1095 | ~0.08 | ~+0.03 |\\n| top-7 EAP-IG | ~0.125 | ~0.10 | ~+0.025 |\\n| top-7 EP | ~0.105 | ~0.09 | ~+0.015 |\\n| top-7 ACDC | ~0.115 | ~0.095 | ~+0.020 |\\n| random-7 | ~0.04 | ~0.02 | ~+0.02 |\\n\"\n100\t      }\n101\t    ],\n102\t    \"figures\": [],\n103\t    \"analysis\": \"Ablation method comparison 在 worst 档下提供了 IOI artifact 的第二条独立证据 （第一条来自 size-controlled baseline）。Zero ablation bias + size confound 双重 artifact 完全解释了 IOI 的表面 PASS。这对论文有利有弊：有利在于 mechanistic 解释 更充分（两条独立 artifact 路径），但代价是 IOI 作为 positive anchor 彻底消失， paper 变为 \\\"pure negative result + failure mode taxonomy\\\"。建议将此结果作为 Appendix 中的 supplementary analysis，主文只在 size-controlled baseline 处 以一句话提及 \\\"ablation method comparison further confirms the size confound\\\"。\\n\\n\\nZero ablation 将移除的 edges 设为零向量，这对小 circuit（如 CSS=1.0 的 7 edges） 天然有利——移除少量 edges 对模型的破坏小，保留的信息多，CPR 高。但这不是 CSS 的 功劳，而是 evaluation metric 对 circuit size 的系统性 bias。在 worst 档下， mean ablation（移除的 edges 设为 dataset-level mean activation）提供更公平的对比， 因为 mean ablation 下保留 7 edges 的 CPR 降幅更大（模型需要真正依赖这 7 条 edges 才能维持性能，而非依赖剩余 32484 条 edges 的 residual 信号）。具体来说，mean ablation 下 CSS=1.0 的 CPR 从 0.1095 降到 ≈0.08，而 top-7 EAP-IG 在 mean ablation 下 CPR ≈0.10（gradient 选出的 top edges 更 faithfully 捕捉了 IOI 电路核心）。 这进一步证实 IOI PASS 是 evaluation artifact 而非 genuine CSS advantage。\\n\"\n104\t  },\n105\t  {\n106\t    \"name\": \"IFR vs ACDC vs gradient method divergence analysis\",\n107\t    \"description\": \"分析 Qwen-0.5B 上 IFR 和 ACDC 各自的 failure mode，作为 component-level scoring scaling failure (Claim 3) 的 case study。纯分析任务，无新实验。\\n\",\n108\t    \"results\": {\n109\t      \"ifr_failure_mode\": \"block-voting — scores at layer granularity, not edge granularity\",\n110\t      \"acdc_failure_mode\": \"node-level scoring — 179K edges collapsed to ~200 node-level decisions\",\n111\t      \"ifr_top100_layer_concentration\": \"95%+ in layers 0-5 (early MLP→attn connections)\",\n112\t      \"acdc_top100_layer_concentration\": \"85%+ in layers 18-23 (late attention heads)\",\n113\t      \"ifr_acdc_overlap\": \"0 shared edges in top-100\",\n114\t      \"gradient_methods_overlap\": \"EAP-IG × EP Jaccard still ~0.54 on Qwen\",\n115\t      \"root_cause_shared\": \"both IFR and ACDC perform component-level (node/block) scoring on large models; edge-level discrimination impossible with 179K candidates\",\n116\t      \"fixability_assessment\": \"not fixable by method substitution — requires architectural change to scoring\",\n117\t      \"experiments_completed_by_deadline\": \"[2, 3]\"\n118\t    },\n119\t    \"tables\": [\n120\t      {\n121\t        \"name\": \"Table: Method Failure Mode Taxonomy on Qwen-0.5B\",\n122\t        \"content\": \"| Method | Scoring Granularity | Top-100 Layer Concentration | Jaccard with Others | Failure Mode |\\n|--------|--------------------|-----------------------------|--------------------:|--------------|\\n| IFR | Block (layer-pair) | 95% in L0-L5 | 0.000 | Block-voting |\\n| ACDC | Node | 85% in L18-L23 | 0.043 | Node-broadcasting |\\n| EAP-IG | Edge (gradient) | ~60% in L10-L20 | 0.540 (w/ EP) | Method correlation |\\n| EP | Edge (gradient) | ~55% in L10-L20 | 0.540 (w/ EAP-IG) | Method correlation |\\n\"\n123\t      }\n124\t    ],\n125\t    \"figures\": [],\n126\t    \"analysis\": \"Divergence analysis 在 worst 档下是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence，也是整篇论文避免被 reviewer 视为 \\\"trivial negative result\\\" 的关键。通过展示 scaling failure 的 mechanistic root cause（component-level scoring bottleneck），我们将 \\\"CSS doesn't work on Qwen\\\" 从一个 data point 提升为一个 generalizable insight：任何依赖 component-level scoring 的 circuit discovery method 在 >100K edges 的模型上 都无法为 consensus 提供有意义的 independent signals。这个 insight 对 community 有 actionable implications——未来的 circuit discovery 方法需要 true edge-level scoring 才能在大模型上支持 multi-method validation。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，divergence analysis 揭示 IFR 和 ACDC 虽然失败模式不同（IFR 是 block-voting， ACDC 是 node-level scoring），但 root cause 相同：这两种方法在设计上都是对 components （nodes/layers）进行评分然后 broadcast 到 edges，而非直接对 edges 评分。在 GPT-2 Small 的 32K edges 上这个 approximation 尚可（ACDC 的 14 isinf edges 仍能捕捉到 IOI 核心）， 但在 Qwen-0.5B 的 179K edges 上，每个 node 下辖 ~1000 edges，node-level 评分导致 要么全选要么全不选，无法做 edge-level 区分。这意味着 scaling failure 不是某个方法的 implementation bug，而是 component-level scoring paradigm 的根本限制。 EAP-IG 和 EP 作为 gradient-based 方法虽然在数学上是 edge-level 的，但它们之间的 高 Jaccard (0.54) 说明 gradient 方法本身也趋于一致，无法提供 consensus 所需的 independent evidence。最终结论是：在大模型上，没有任何现有方法组合能使 binary consensus 有效工作——要么方法不够 edge-level (IFR, ACDC)，要么方法太相似 (EAP-IG, EP)。这是 universal failure 在 scaling 维度上的 mechanistic 解释。\\n\"\n127\t  },\n128\t  {\n129\t    \"name\": \"Jaccard-CSS scatter plot + correlation\",\n130\t    \"description\": \"汇总所有实验的 max pairwise Jaccard vs CSS CPR advantage，绘制 scatter plot 并报告 correlation。原计划用于支持 Claim 4 (Jaccard diagnostic)。\\n\",\n131\t    \"results\": {\n132\t      \"n_datapoints\": \"[5, 6]\",\n133\t      \"datapoints\": [\n134\t        {\n135\t          \"label\": \"IOI GPT-2\",\n136\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.31,\n137\t          \"css_advantage\": \"[-0.01, 0.02] (size-controlled, no longer PASS)\"\n138\t        },\n139\t        {\n140\t          \"label\": \"Arithmetic GPT-2\",\n141\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.695,\n142\t          \"css_advantage\": -0.066\n143\t        },\n144\t        {\n145\t          \"label\": \"SVA GPT-2\",\n146\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.653,\n147\t          \"css_advantage\": \"[0.00, 0.013] (not significant)\"\n148\t        },\n149\t        {\n150\t          \"label\": \"Factual Recall GPT-2\",\n151\t          \"max_jaccard\": \"[0.10, 0.50]\",\n152\t          \"css_advantage\": \"[-0.20, -0.05]\"\n153\t        },\n154\t        {\n155\t          \"label\": \"IOI Qwen (IFR)\",\n156\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.54,\n157\t          \"css_advantage\": \"N/A (0 CSS edges)\"\n158\t        },\n159\t        {\n160\t          \"label\": \"IOI Qwen (ACDC)\",\n161\t          \"max_jaccard\": 0.043,\n162\t          \"css_advantage\": -0.05\n163\t        }\n164\t      ],\n165\t      \"pearson_r\": \"undefined or near 0\",\n166\t      \"spearman_rho\": \"undefined or near 0\",\n167\t      \"claim4_verdict\": \"DELETED — no PASS calibration point, scatter shows no interpretable pattern\",\n168\t      \"jaccard_diagnostic_accuracy\": null\n169\t    },\n170\t    \"tables\": [\n171\t      {\n172\t        \"name\": \"Table: Jaccard vs CSS Advantage Summary (all configs)\",\n173\t        \"content\": \"| Config | max Jaccard | CSS Δ (size-ctrl) | Significant? |\\n|--------|-----------|-------------------|-------------|\\n| IOI GPT-2 | 0.31 | +0.01 | No |\\n| Arithmetic GPT-2 | 0.70 | −0.07 | Yes (neg) |\\n| SVA GPT-2 | 0.65 | +0.01 | No |\\n| Factual Recall GPT-2 | ~0.35 | −0.11 | Yes (neg) |\\n| IOI Qwen (IFR) | 0.54 | N/A | — |\\n| IOI Qwen (ACDC) | 0.04 | −0.05 | Yes (neg) |\\n\"\n174\t      }\n175\t    ],\n176\t    \"figures\": [],\n177\t    \"analysis\": \"Scatter plot 在 worst 档下从 Claim 4 的支撑证据变为 universal failure 的补充 可视化。原来的 \\\"low Jaccard → CSS helps\\\" 假设完全不成立：Qwen-ACDC 有最低的 Jaccard (0.04) 但 CSS advantage 为负，因为 scaling failure (Claim 3) 与 Jaccard level 无关——即使方法之间完全 independent (Jaccard≈0)，如果各方法 都在做 component-level scoring 而非 edge-level scoring，consensus 仍然无意义。 这实际上是一个重要的 negative finding：Jaccard 不是 sufficient diagnostic—— 即使 Jaccard 很低（方法确实独立），consensus 仍可能无用，因为 \\\"independent but all wrong\\\" 不比 \\\"correlated and all wrong\\\" 更好。但这个 insight 太 subtle 且 n 太小，不足以支撑一个独立 claim，只适合作为 Discussion 中的一段话。\\n\\n在 worst 档下，IOI 从 PASS 变为 artifact（size-controlled Δ ≈ 0），意味着 scatter plot 上没有任何 positive CSS advantage 的数据点。原来的 Claim 4 假设是 \\\"low Jaccard → CSS helps, high Jaccard → CSS doesn't help\\\"，但现在所有点都在 Y ≤ 0 区域（CSS advantage ≤ 0），无论 Jaccard 高低。IOI (Jaccard=0.31) 和 Qwen-ACDC (Jaccard=0.043) 都是 low Jaccard 但 CSS advantage ≈ 0 或负，打破了 \\\"low Jaccard → CSS helps\\\" 的 假设。scatter plot 变成了一个没有 pattern 的点云：所有点都在零线以下或附近， Jaccard 值从 0.04 到 0.70 均无 positive advantage。Pearson/Spearman 相关系数 接近 0 或 undefined（variance 太小）。Claim 4 必须从 paper 中删除，因为没有 PASS calibration point 就不可能建立 \\\"diagnostic threshold\\\" 的概念。scatter plot 可以保留在 Appendix 作为 \\\"confirming universal failure across Jaccard spectrum\\\" 的补充证据，但不能再作为独立 claim。\\n\"\n178\t  }\n179\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5877df95-69bb-4cfc-9f89-ab867711b59f","uuid":"3f406f06-b536-4088-b1aa-1f45565e6734","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:50:17.187Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T092135/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GPT-2 Factual Recall K=3 CSS\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-2 Small 上的 Country-Capital factual recall 任务，K=3 methods (EAP-IG + EP + ACDC)。 MLP-based knowledge retrieval circuit，测试 CSS 在知识提取类电路上的表现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"FAIL_or_CRASH\",\n      \"css_3of3_edges\": 0,\n      \"css_2of3_edges\": \"[5, 25]\",\n      \"css_1of3_edges\": \"[70, 120]\",\n      \"pairwise_jaccard_max\": \"[0.05, 0.20]\",\n      \"pairwise_jaccard_eapig_ep\": \"[0.35, 0.55]\",\n      \"pairwise_jaccard_eapig_acdc\": \"[0.02, 0.10]\",\n      \"pairwise_jaccard_ep_acdc\": \"[0.02, 0.10]\",\n      \"acdc_edges_isinf\": \"[3, 12]\",\n      \"mean_cpr_css_1.00\": \"N/A or negative\",\n      \"mean_cpr_best_single\": \"[0.85, 1.05]\",\n      \"d025_cond4_css_gt_single\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"d025_verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"crash_probability\": \"30%\",\n      \"factual_recall_css_vs_best_single_delta\": \"[-0.20, -0.05]\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Factual Recall D025 Gate Conditions\",\n        \"content\": \"| Condition | Criterion | Result | Value |\\n|-----------|-----------|--------|-------|\\n| C1: Jaccard < 0.70 | max pairwise < 0.70 | PASS | 0.48 |\\n| C2: CSS≥2/3 ≥ 10 | count ≥ 10 | FAIL | 8 |\\n| C3: CSS=1.0 ≥ 3 | count ≥ 3 | FAIL | 0 |\\n| C4: CSS > single | CPR dominance | FAIL | N/A |\\n| **Overall** | | **FAIL** | |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Factual recall FAIL 将实验配置计数从 1/5 PASS 推向 1/6 PASS（若 size-controlled 也 FAIL 则为 0/6）。更重要的是，这是第一个 MLP-centric task，FAIL 表明 CSS 不仅在 attention-heavy circuits (IOI) 上偶尔成功、在其他 attention circuits (Arithmetic, SVA) 上失败，而是在 circuit 拓扑类型上也 universally 失败。这消除了 \\\"CSS works for attention circuits but not MLP circuits\\\" 这种 nuanced 叙事的可能性，强化了 universal failure 结论。\\n\\n\\nFactual recall 电路高度依赖 MLP 层中的 knowledge neurons，电路结构与 IOI 的 attention-head-dominated 拓扑完全不同。在 worst 档下有两种 FAIL 路径： (路径 A) ACDC 在 factual recall 上的 isinf binarization 产生极少 edges（3-12 条）， 这些 edges 集中在特定 MLP-to-residual 连接上，与 EAP-IG/EP 的 gradient-based top-k 选择几乎无交集（Jaccard ≈ 0.05），导致 CSS=1.0 edges 为 0 或极少且非关键； (路径 B) v2 修复了 v1 的 crash 但引入了新的数据加载或 evaluation 问题导致 实验直接失败（30% 概率），鉴于 v1 已经 crashed。即使 v2 成功运行，factual recall 的 MLP-centric 电路拓扑意味着 gradient-adjacent methods (EAP-IG, EP) 之间的 Jaccard 仍然偏高（0.35-0.55），形成类似 Arithmetic 的 method-correlation 问题， CSS=1.0 退化为 ACDC 单方法输出但 ACDC 本身 CPR 不佳，CSS advantage delta 为负。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"IOI size-controlled baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"IOI 上 CSS=1.0 (7 edges) 与 size-controlled baselines 对比：top-7 of EAP-IG, top-7 of EP, top-7 of ACDC, random-7。排除 IOI PASS 结果是否仅因 CSS 选出了更少 edges 的 size confound。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"css_1.00_cpr\": 0.1095,\n      \"top7_eapig_cpr\": \"[0.10, 0.15]\",\n      \"top7_ep_cpr\": \"[0.08, 0.13]\",\n      \"top7_acdc_cpr\": \"[0.09, 0.14]\",\n      \"random7_cpr_mean\": \"[0.02, 0.06]\",\n      \"random7_cpr_std\": \"[0.03, 0.08]\",\n      \"css_advantage_over_best_single_top7\": \"[-0.04, 0.01]\",\n      \"size_controlled_ioi_css_advantage_retained_pct\": \"[0, 20]\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CSS advantage dissolved — size confound confirmed\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: IOI Size-Controlled CPR Comparison (7 edges each)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Circuit | Edges | CPR (mean abl.) | Δ vs CSS=1.0 |\\n|---------|-------|-----------------|--------------|\\n| CSS=1.0 | 7 | 0.1095 | — |\\n| top-7 EAP-IG | 7 | ~0.125 | +0.016 |\\n| top-7 EP | 7 | ~0.105 | −0.005 |\\n| top-7 ACDC | 7 | ~0.115 | +0.006 |\\n| random-7 (mean±std) | 7 | ~0.04±0.05 | −0.070 |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Size-controlled baseline 是 worst 档的关键 pivot。一旦确认 IOI 的 CSS 优势可被 size confound 完全解释，IOI 从 \\\"lone PASS\\\" 变为 \\\"apparent PASS that is actually artifact\\\"， 总计 0/6 PASS。这从根本上改变了 paper 的叙事：不再是 \\\"consensus mostly fails (1/6)\\\" 而是 \\\"consensus never helps (0/6)\\\"。好处是结论更强更clean；坏处是失去了 IOI 作为 positive calibration point 的解释力，Claim 4 (Jaccard diagnostic) 因为没有任何 PASS 数据点而 完全无法校准，必须删除或降为 \\\"future work with more tasks\\\" 一句话。\\n\\n\\nIOI 上 CSS=1.0 的 7 edges 恰好是 ACDC isinf 选出的 14 edges 中同时被 EAP-IG 或 EP top-100 覆盖的子集。在 worst 档下，当我们将 EAP-IG 和 EP 也限制为 top-7 edges 时， 这些 top-7 edges 大概率落在 IOI 电路的核心 attention heads (name movers, S-inhibition heads) 上——这些 heads 在所有方法中都获得最高分数。因此 top-7 EAP-IG 的 CPR 会达到 0.10-0.15（甚至超过 CSS=1.0 的 0.1095），因为 gradient 方法对这些 heads 的排序 本身就是准确的，CSS 并没有提供额外的过滤信号。ACDC top-7 同理（0.09-0.14）。 Random-7 作为 null baseline 仍然显著更差（CPR 0.02-0.06），说明电路信号存在， 但这是方法本身的功劳而非 consensus 的功劳。CSS=1.0 的 CPR 优势从原始的 +0.08 (vs ACDC full-14) 缩小到 Δ ≈ [-0.04, +0.01]，即统计上为零。 这意味着 IOI 的 \\\"PASS\\\" 本质上是 size artifact——CSS 恰好选出了更少的 edges， 而在 circuit evaluation 中 fewer-but-correct edges 天然有 CPR 优势（less noise）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bootstrap confidence intervals on CPR\",\n    \"description\": \"对所有已完成实验的 CPR differences 计算 bootstrap 95% CIs（B=10000）。 重点：IOI CSS=1.0 vs best single method Δ, SVA D032 marginal PASS Δ=0.0127。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ioi_css_vs_best_single_delta_point\": 0.0127,\n      \"ioi_css_vs_best_single_delta_ci_lower\": \"[-0.05, -0.01]\",\n      \"ioi_css_vs_best_single_delta_ci_upper\": \"[0.05, 0.08]\",\n      \"ioi_css_vs_best_single_p_value\": \"[0.15, 0.45]\",\n      \"ioi_cpr_delta_ci_lower\": \"[-0.05, -0.01]\",\n      \"ioi_cpr_delta_point\": \"[-0.02, 0.03]\",\n      \"sva_d032_delta_point\": 0.0127,\n      \"sva_d032_delta_ci_lower\": \"[-0.03, -0.005]\",\n      \"sva_d032_delta_ci_upper\": \"[0.03, 0.06]\",\n      \"sva_d032_p_value\": \"[0.20, 0.55]\",\n      \"arithmetic_css_vs_eapig_delta_ci\": \"fully negative, confirming FAIL\",\n      \"qwen_ioi_ifr_delta_ci\": \"fully negative or undefined (0 CSS edges)\",\n      \"qwen_ioi_acdc_delta_ci\": \"fully negative or undefined (0 CSS edges)\",\n      \"significant_advantages_count\": 0,\n      \"total_tests\": \"[5, 6]\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Bootstrap 95% CIs for CPR Δ (CSS=1.0 vs Best Single Method)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Task × Model | Δ point | 95% CI | p-value | Significant? |\\n|-------------|---------|--------|---------|-------------|\\n| IOI GPT-2 (size-ctrl) | +0.012 | [−0.03, +0.06] | 0.31 | No |\\n| Arithmetic GPT-2 | −0.066 | [−0.12, −0.02] | 0.005 | Yes (negative) |\\n| SVA GPT-2 | +0.013 | [−0.02, +0.05] | 0.28 | No |\\n| Factual Recall GPT-2 | −0.11 | [−0.19, −0.04] | 0.002 | Yes (negative) |\\n| IOI Qwen (IFR) | N/A | N/A | N/A | 0 CSS edges |\\n| IOI Qwen (ACDC) | −0.05 | [−0.09, −0.01] | 0.01 | Yes (negative) |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bootstrap CIs 是 worst 档叙事的统计 backbone。它将 \\\"IOI PASS\\\" 和 \\\"SVA marginal PASS\\\" 同时去 significant 化，使得 reviewer 无法反驳 \\\"0/N significant positive advantages\\\" 的 结论。同时 Arithmetic 和 Qwen 的 significantly negative Δ 强化了 \\\"CSS can actively hurt\\\" 的 sub-claim。风险在于 reviewer 可能认为 \\\"method A is not significantly better than method B\\\" 是 trivially expected（多数 ensemble 方法在小样本下都不显著），需要在 Discussion 中论证 community 对 consensus 的 implicit assumption 来建立 contribution。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CIs 在 worst 档下证实所有表面上的 CSS 优势都不显著。IOI 的原始 CSS=1.0 CPR=0.1095 vs ACDC CPR=0.0286 看似有 Δ=0.08 优势，但这个 Δ 是 在 7 edges vs 14 edges 的不公平对比下得到的。在 size-controlled 框架下 （plan_008 已证实 size confound），Δ 缩小到 ≈0.01-0.03，此时 bootstrap 重采样的 variance 来自 IOI prompt 样本间的 CPR 变异——由于 IOI 数据集 只有 ~100 个样本对，且 circuit 极小（7 edges），每次重采样的 CPR 波动较大 （std ≈ 0.03-0.05），导致 95% CI 跨零且宽（[-0.05, 0.08]），p > 0.15。 SVA 的 Δ=0.0127 本身就在 noise floor 级别，bootstrap CI 必然跨零。 Arithmetic 和 Qwen 实验的 CSS Δ 本身为负，CIs 确认这些是 genuine FAILs。 最终结果：0/5-6 个配置有 statistically significant CSS advantage。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Ablation method comparison (zero vs mean)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 IOI 上对比 zero ablation 和 mean ablation 的 CPR 评估。Dream worst-tier 识别出 zero ablation 可能偏向 smaller circuits (IOI CSS=1.0 的 7 edges)， 需要排除 evaluation metric 本身的 bias。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"zero_abl_css_1.00_cpr\": 0.1095,\n      \"zero_abl_top7_eapig_cpr\": \"[0.10, 0.14]\",\n      \"zero_abl_css_advantage\": \"[-0.03, 0.01]\",\n      \"mean_abl_css_1.00_cpr\": \"[0.06, 0.10]\",\n      \"mean_abl_top7_eapig_cpr\": \"[0.08, 0.12]\",\n      \"mean_abl_css_advantage\": \"[-0.06, -0.01]\",\n      \"zero_vs_mean_gap_for_small_circuits\": \"[0.02, 0.05]\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"zero ablation inflates small-circuit CPR; mean ablation shows CSS disadvantage\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Zero vs Mean Ablation CPR on IOI (7 edges)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Circuit (7 edges) | Zero Abl CPR | Mean Abl CPR | Δ(zero−mean) |\\n|-------------------|-------------|-------------|--------------|\\n| CSS=1.0 | 0.1095 | ~0.08 | ~+0.03 |\\n| top-7 EAP-IG | ~0.125 | ~0.10 | ~+0.025 |\\n| top-7 EP | ~0.105 | ~0.09 | ~+0.015 |\\n| top-7 ACDC | ~0.115 | ~0.095 | ~+0.020 |\\n| random-7 | ~0.04 | ~0.02 | ~+0.02 |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Ablation method comparison 在 worst 档下提供了 IOI artifact 的第二条独立证据 （第一条来自 size-controlled baseline）。Zero ablation bias + size confound 双重 artifact 完全解释了 IOI 的表面 PASS。这对论文有利有弊：有利在于 mechanistic 解释 更充分（两条独立 artifact 路径），但代价是 IOI 作为 positive anchor 彻底消失， paper 变为 \\\"pure negative result + failure mode taxonomy\\\"。建议将此结果作为 Appendix 中的 supplementary analysis，主文只在 size-controlled baseline 处 以一句话提及 \\\"ablation method comparison further confirms the size confound\\\"。\\n\\n\\nZero ablation 将移除的 edges 设为零向量，这对小 circuit（如 CSS=1.0 的 7 edges） 天然有利——移除少量 edges 对模型的破坏小，保留的信息多，CPR 高。但这不是 CSS 的 功劳，而是 evaluation metric 对 circuit size 的系统性 bias。在 worst 档下， mean ablation（移除的 edges 设为 dataset-level mean activation）提供更公平的对比， 因为 mean ablation 下保留 7 edges 的 CPR 降幅更大（模型需要真正依赖这 7 条 edges 才能维持性能，而非依赖剩余 32484 条 edges 的 residual 信号）。具体来说，mean ablation 下 CSS=1.0 的 CPR 从 0.1095 降到 ≈0.08，而 top-7 EAP-IG 在 mean ablation 下 CPR ≈0.10（gradient 选出的 top edges 更 faithfully 捕捉了 IOI 电路核心）。 这进一步证实 IOI PASS 是 evaluation artifact 而非 genuine CSS advantage。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"IFR vs ACDC vs gradient method divergence analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 Qwen-0.5B 上 IFR 和 ACDC 各自的 failure mode，作为 component-level scoring scaling failure (Claim 3) 的 case study。纯分析任务，无新实验。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ifr_failure_mode\": \"block-voting — scores at layer granularity, not edge granularity\",\n      \"acdc_failure_mode\": \"node-level scoring — 179K edges collapsed to ~200 node-level decisions\",\n      \"ifr_top100_layer_concentration\": \"95%+ in layers 0-5 (early MLP→attn connections)\",\n      \"acdc_top100_layer_concentration\": \"85%+ in layers 18-23 (late attention heads)\",\n      \"ifr_acdc_overlap\": \"0 shared edges in top-100\",\n      \"gradient_methods_overlap\": \"EAP-IG × EP Jaccard still ~0.54 on Qwen\",\n      \"root_cause_shared\": \"both IFR and ACDC perform component-level (node/block) scoring on large models; edge-level discrimination impossible with 179K candidates\",\n      \"fixability_assessment\": \"not fixable by method substitution — requires architectural change to scoring\",\n      \"experiments_completed_by_deadline\": \"[2, 3]\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Method Failure Mode Taxonomy on Qwen-0.5B\",\n        \"content\": \"| Method | Scoring Granularity | Top-100 Layer Concentration | Jaccard with Others | Failure Mode |\\n|--------|--------------------|-----------------------------|--------------------:|--------------|\\n| IFR | Block (layer-pair) | 95% in L0-L5 | 0.000 | Block-voting |\\n| ACDC | Node | 85% in L18-L23 | 0.043 | Node-broadcasting |\\n| EAP-IG | Edge (gradient) | ~60% in L10-L20 | 0.540 (w/ EP) | Method correlation |\\n| EP | Edge (gradient) | ~55% in L10-L20 | 0.540 (w/ EAP-IG) | Method correlation |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Divergence analysis 在 worst 档下是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence，也是整篇论文避免被 reviewer 视为 \\\"trivial negative result\\\" 的关键。通过展示 scaling failure 的 mechanistic root cause（component-level scoring bottleneck），我们将 \\\"CSS doesn't work on Qwen\\\" 从一个 data point 提升为一个 generalizable insight：任何依赖 component-level scoring 的 circuit discovery method 在 >100K edges 的模型上 都无法为 consensus 提供有意义的 independent signals。这个 insight 对 community 有 actionable implications——未来的 circuit discovery 方法需要 true edge-level scoring 才能在大模型上支持 multi-method validation。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，divergence analysis 揭示 IFR 和 ACDC 虽然失败模式不同（IFR 是 block-voting， ACDC 是 node-level scoring），但 root cause 相同：这两种方法在设计上都是对 components （nodes/layers）进行评分然后 broadcast 到 edges，而非直接对 edges 评分。在 GPT-2 Small 的 32K edges 上这个 approximation 尚可（ACDC 的 14 isinf edges 仍能捕捉到 IOI 核心）， 但在 Qwen-0.5B 的 179K edges 上，每个 node 下辖 ~1000 edges，node-level 评分导致 要么全选要么全不选，无法做 edge-level 区分。这意味着 scaling failure 不是某个方法的 implementation bug，而是 component-level scoring paradigm 的根本限制。 EAP-IG 和 EP 作为 gradient-based 方法虽然在数学上是 edge-level 的，但它们之间的 高 Jaccard (0.54) 说明 gradient 方法本身也趋于一致，无法提供 consensus 所需的 independent evidence。最终结论是：在大模型上，没有任何现有方法组合能使 binary consensus 有效工作——要么方法不够 edge-level (IFR, ACDC)，要么方法太相似 (EAP-IG, EP)。这是 universal failure 在 scaling 维度上的 mechanistic 解释。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Jaccard-CSS scatter plot + correlation\",\n    \"description\": \"汇总所有实验的 max pairwise Jaccard vs CSS CPR advantage，绘制 scatter plot 并报告 correlation。原计划用于支持 Claim 4 (Jaccard diagnostic)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_datapoints\": \"[5, 6]\",\n      \"datapoints\": [\n        {\n          \"label\": \"IOI GPT-2\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.31,\n          \"css_advantage\": \"[-0.01, 0.02] (size-controlled, no longer PASS)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"label\": \"Arithmetic GPT-2\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.695,\n          \"css_advantage\": -0.066\n        },\n        {\n          \"label\": \"SVA GPT-2\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.653,\n          \"css_advantage\": \"[0.00, 0.013] (not significant)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"label\": \"Factual Recall GPT-2\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": \"[0.10, 0.50]\",\n          \"css_advantage\": \"[-0.20, -0.05]\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"label\": \"IOI Qwen (IFR)\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.54,\n          \"css_advantage\": \"N/A (0 CSS edges)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"label\": \"IOI Qwen (ACDC)\",\n          \"max_jaccard\": 0.043,\n          \"css_advantage\": -0.05\n        }\n      ],\n      \"pearson_r\": \"undefined or near 0\",\n      \"spearman_rho\": \"undefined or near 0\",\n      \"claim4_verdict\": \"DELETED — no PASS calibration point, scatter shows no interpretable pattern\",\n      \"jaccard_diagnostic_accuracy\": null\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Jaccard vs CSS Advantage Summary (all configs)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Config | max Jaccard | CSS Δ (size-ctrl) | Significant? |\\n|--------|-----------|-------------------|-------------|\\n| IOI GPT-2 | 0.31 | +0.01 | No |\\n| Arithmetic GPT-2 | 0.70 | −0.07 | Yes (neg) |\\n| SVA GPT-2 | 0.65 | +0.01 | No |\\n| Factual Recall GPT-2 | ~0.35 | −0.11 | Yes (neg) |\\n| IOI Qwen (IFR) | 0.54 | N/A | — |\\n| IOI Qwen (ACDC) | 0.04 | −0.05 | Yes (neg) |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Scatter plot 在 worst 档下从 Claim 4 的支撑证据变为 universal failure 的补充 可视化。原来的 \\\"low Jaccard → CSS helps\\\" 假设完全不成立：Qwen-ACDC 有最低的 Jaccard (0.04) 但 CSS advantage 为负，因为 scaling failure (Claim 3) 与 Jaccard level 无关——即使方法之间完全 independent (Jaccard≈0)，如果各方法 都在做 component-level scoring 而非 edge-level scoring，consensus 仍然无意义。 这实际上是一个重要的 negative finding：Jaccard 不是 sufficient diagnostic—— 即使 Jaccard 很低（方法确实独立），consensus 仍可能无用，因为 \\\"independent but all wrong\\\" 不比 \\\"correlated and all wrong\\\" 更好。但这个 insight 太 subtle 且 n 太小，不足以支撑一个独立 claim，只适合作为 Discussion 中的一段话。\\n\\n在 worst 档下，IOI 从 PASS 变为 artifact（size-controlled Δ ≈ 0），意味着 scatter plot 上没有任何 positive CSS advantage 的数据点。原来的 Claim 4 假设是 \\\"low Jaccard → CSS helps, high Jaccard → CSS doesn't help\\\"，但现在所有点都在 Y ≤ 0 区域（CSS advantage ≤ 0），无论 Jaccard 高低。IOI (Jaccard=0.31) 和 Qwen-ACDC (Jaccard=0.043) 都是 low Jaccard 但 CSS advantage ≈ 0 或负，打破了 \\\"low Jaccard → CSS helps\\\" 的 假设。scatter plot 变成了一个没有 pattern 的点云：所有点都在零线以下或附近， Jaccard 值从 0.04 到 0.70 均无 positive advantage。Pearson/Spearman 相关系数 接近 0 或 undefined（variance 太小）。Claim 4 必须从 paper 中删除，因为没有 PASS calibration point 就不可能建立 \\\"diagnostic threshold\\\" 的概念。scatter plot 可以保留在 Appendix 作为 \\\"confirming universal failure across Jaccard spectrum\\\" 的补充证据，但不能再作为独立 claim。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":179,"startLine":1,"totalLines":179}}}
